{
 "case": "SRC-04",
 "says": "A person with no Team installs a product-supplied knowledge package into their own scope through the add_published_package route (source.revision.admit), naming the exact revision by the digest of the publisher's manifest. The owner commits it and returns that same manifest and a provenance whose origin is the product-supplied package with its publisher evidence, whose acceptance is not_accepted, and which keeps the package's illustrative ADR statements (author, decision date, status Accepted, a council approval) as stated_only claims. The person registers the publisher-owned home (package_published, the package id and license conditions) and resolves an exact member back to the same manifest, provenance and that member's own bytes, with the publisher-owned home as it stands at the head the registration left. Negative: a commit of a manifest that edits a publisher member in place is refused with publisher_bytes_modified and nothing changes; installing records no Team acceptance, adoption or history, and asking the person's memory state for the decision the illustrative ADR describes returns no entry, because an example ADR in a package is not a past choice of this person or any Team.",
